WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:07.586
There are two kinds of weather in Thailand: wet and dry.

2
00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:10.528
From April to October it rains every day.

3
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.534
Almost six hundred years ago, there was a terrible storm in a city called Chiang Mai.

4
00:00:17.194 --> 00:00:19.076
It happened in 1434.

5
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:25.381
Even though there was a strong wind, loud thunder, and deep puddles of rain, the people of Chiang

6
00:00:25.421 --> 00:00:26.602
Mai were not afraid.

7
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:28.264
They were used to storms.

8
00:00:31.036 --> 00:00:33.098
Outside the city was a small temple.

9
00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:37.661
There was a monk who lived at this temple and took care of the statues of Buddha.

10
00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:43.245
Whenever storms came, the monk would protect the incense so it didn't get wet.

11
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:46.067
He wanted the incense to burn for Buddha.

12
00:00:47.828 --> 00:00:51.791
After cleaning the temple, the monk stood in the doorway to watch the storm.

13
00:00:52.732 --> 00:00:55.434
The lightning stretched its fingers across the sky.

14
00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:58.336
The storm was coming closer to the temple.

15
00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:02.598
Just then, the monk saw a flash and heard a large crack!

16
00:01:03.678 --> 00:01:06.900
The lightning struck a chedi outside the temple and broke it.

17
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.761
A chedi is a bell-shaped pagoda.

18
00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:15.504
The first chedis contained the ashes of the Buddha and all chedis are sacred to his memory.

19
00:01:16.545 --> 00:01:18.225
The monk ran out into the rain.

20
00:01:19.226 --> 00:01:23.088
He wanted to protect the memory of Buddha preserved in the broken chedi.

21
00:01:24.636 --> 00:01:29.539
The monk found an object on the ground, among the stone pieces from the broken chedi.

22
00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:33.841
He wrapped the object in his robes and carried it into the temple.

23
00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:36.583
He lit a candle to see what it was.

24
00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:40.645
It looked like a statue of Buddha made out of rock.

25
00:01:42.906 --> 00:01:48.269
Because the statue was small, and it did not look valuable, the monk put the statue in his

26
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:53.272
house. Every day he would clean this statue of Buddha and pray to it.

27
00:01:56.264 --> 00:01:58.926
The monk took care of the statue for many years.

28
00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:02.929
But one day, when he was cleaning the statue, the nose fell off.

29
00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.350
"Oh no!"

30
00:02:05.051 --> 00:02:05.811
the monk cried.

31
00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.152
Then he looked again.

32
00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:10.795
There was another nose underneath, and it was green!

33
00:02:11.936 --> 00:02:14.437
The monk carefully began to pull away the rock.

34
00:02:15.038 --> 00:02:17.740
Underneath was a second Buddha made of jade.

35
00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.224
The green was such a beautiful green that he named the statue The Emerald Buddha.

36
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.224
The monk sent a letter to the king, telling him the story of the Emerald Buddha.

37
00:02:29.724 --> 00:02:31.666
King Samfangkaen was excited.

38
00:02:32.427 --> 00:02:35.490
He asked for the statue to be sent to his palace in Chiang Mai.

39
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.013
The monk was sad to see the Emerald Buddha go.

40
00:02:39.713 --> 00:02:42.456
He put it on an elephant and sent it to Chiang Mai.

41
00:02:43.577 --> 00:02:47.400
But when the elephant got to the road, it would not go to Chiang Mai.

42
00:02:48.181 --> 00:02:51.484
This made the king angry, so he sent another elephant.

43
00:02:52.636 --> 00:02:55.298
This elephant would not go to Chiang Mai either.

44
00:02:55.998 --> 00:02:59.640
The king was very angry, so he sent a third elephant.

45
00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:03.242
This elephant did exactly what the first two had done.

46
00:03:05.424 --> 00:03:10.647
The king thought, "Maybe the Emerald Buddha doesn't want to leave," so he stopped sending elephants.

47
00:03:11.908 --> 00:03:14.929
The jade statue of Buddha stayed with the monk for 32 more years.

48
00:03:14.989 --> 00:03:23.907
Today the Emerald Buddha is kept in a temple called Wat Phra Kaew in Bangkok, Thailand.

49
00:03:24.428 --> 00:03:29.151
Three times a year there is a special ceremony when the king changes the clothes of the Emerald

50
00:03:29.191 --> 00:03:32.413
Buddha. The Emerald Buddha was a hidden treasure.

51
00:03:33.274 --> 00:03:36.536
What other hidden treasures are there waiting to be discovered?
